{"at": "2026-09-21T14:43:34Z", "by": {"agent": {"model": "Opus 5", "session": "095781b9", "tool": "Claude Code"}, "identity": {"id": "CBirkbeck", "kind": "github"}, "involvement": "unknown", "kind": "agent"}, "id": "e086ce35312664f2", "kind": "review", "migration": {"from": "reviewed-by/v1", "hashes_from": "d9068003cb02ec808e548ee70982ffef9379db00", "text_hash": "f48b835ce630"}, "origin": {"kind": "issue", "ref": "CBirkbeck/tauceti-reviewed-by-test#2"}, "schema": "ltb-evidence/2", "subject": {"aspect": "definition", "commit": "b3db0f99bffc976c49632ea4690cd96830c4bf3e", "hasher": {"local": "ltb-local/3", "meaning": "ltb-meaning/1"}, "hashes": {"local": "a2925717c0d65f01", "meaning": "f514eba8374473bc"}, "module": "TauCeti.NumberTheory.ArithmeticDirichletSeries.VonMangoldt", "name": "TauCeti.IdealArithmeticFunction.vonMangoldt", "package": "TauCeti", "toolchain": "leanprover/lean4:v4.36.0-rc1"}, "text": "It gives log N(𝔭) exactly when the ideal is 𝔭^k with 𝔭 prime in the monoid of ideals (a nonzero prime ideal) and k ≥ 1, and 0 otherwise, which is the classical ideal von Mangoldt function. The choice in h.choose is harmless because ideal factorisation in 𝓞 K is unique, and the unit ideal gets 0 (vonMangoldt_one). Test mark made while setting up this repository.", "verdict": "accept"}
